-    "content": "# \ud83d\udc4dkanban: Executive Architecture and System Overview\n\nWelcome to the authoritative technical documentation and wiki for **\ud83d\udc4dkanban** (`thumbs-up-kanban`), an open-source, enterprise-grade project management, ticketing, and knowledge platform built from the ground up on two fundamental pillars:\n1. **Security-First (Priority 0):** Hardened zero-trust infrastructure, PostgreSQL Row-Level Security (`FORCE RLS`), five-tier network isolation, AAL2 administrative authorization, and hostile input sanitization.\n2. **Agent-First (Priority 1):** Purpose-built for autonomous AI agents and human teams alike, replacing the context-bloating CRUD-wrapper anti-pattern with an intent-driven, three-surface Model Context Protocol (MCP) server, deterministic workflow gates, and sub-second execution loops.\n\nLicensed under the strictly permissive **Apache-2.0** license, \ud83d\udc4dkanban eliminates SaaS AI paywalls and per-seat subscription lock-in while competing globally against Jira, Vibe Kanban, and commercial issue trackers with drop-in enterprise migration support.\n\n---\n\n## System Topology\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart TD\n    subgraph Clients[\"Client Surfaces\"]\n        SPA[\"React 19 SPA (Desktop, Tablet, Mobile)\"]\n        Agents[\"Autonomous Agents (Cursor, Claude, Codex, Agy)\"]\n    end\n\n    subgraph Entrypoints[\"API & Protocol Gateways\"]\n        FastAPI[\"FastAPI Application Server<br/>- Multi-Card Auth (AAL2)<br/>- Canonical Markdown Pipe<br/>- WebSocket Realtime Hub<br/>- REST API (184 routes)\"]\n        MCP[\"3-Surface MCP Server<br/>- /mcp/agent (9 tools)<br/>- /mcp/docs (6 tools)<br/>- /mcp/admin (12 tools)<br/>- InlineSafeDumper YAML\"]\n    end\n\n    subgraph Core[\"Database Engine & Object Graph\"]\n        UOG[\"Universal Object Graph (UOG)<br/>PostgreSQL 16 with FORCE ROW LEVEL SECURITY (100%)<br/>- Typed object_links, Spine records, Append-only Ledger<br/>- ltree Hierarchical Docs, pgvector Embeddings, Full-Text<br/>- Invalid Object Link Auditor & Purger\"]\n    end\n\n    subgraph Runtimes[\"Execution Engines\"]\n        AIEngine[\"AI Engine & Orchestration<br/>- OpenAI, Ollama, Gemini<br/>- agy -p, codex -p pipes<br/>- Async Gate Helpers\"]\n        Sandbox[\"Sandbox Execution Runtime<br/>- Tier A: Wasmtime engine<br/>- Tier B: nsjail runner<br/>- Scoped Ephemeral Tokens\"]\n    end\n\n    SPA -->|HTTP / WebSocket| FastAPI\n    Agents -->|HTTP / SSE / STDIO| MCP\n    Agents -->|HTTP REST| FastAPI\n    FastAPI --> Core\n    MCP --> Core\n    Core --> AIEngine\n    Core --> Sandbox\n```\n\n---\n\n## Visual Tour: Platform Highlights\n\n### Enterprise Workspace and Project Hub\nThe workspace home delivers clear project visibility, team velocity metrics, and seamless multi-project navigation with responsive layouts across desktop, tablet, and mobile displays.\n\n![Workspace Home and Project Overview](images/05-workspace-home.png)\n\n### Breathable Whitespace Board and High-Contrast Theming\nThe core Kanban board features sub-16ms smooth drag-and-drop, semantic emoji hints, configurable WIP limits, and an enterprise dark theme for reduced eye strain during extended operational sessions.\n\n![Enterprise Whitespace Board View](images/06-board-view.png)\n\n![Dark Theme Enterprise Kanban Board](images/22-dark-theme-board.png)\n\n### Keyboard-Driven Command Palette\nGlobal keyboard shortcuts (`Ctrl+K` / `Cmd+K`) provide instant fuzzy navigation across tickets, documents, projects, and administrative studios without context switching.\n\n![Global Command Palette Navigation](images/23-command-palette.png)\n\n### Multi-View Projections: Table Inline Editing and Timeline Dependencies\nEngineers can switch instantly between Kanban Board, 3-pane List, Table with capability-gated inline cell editing, Calendar, and Timeline with SVG Bezier BLOCKS dependency arrows.\n\n![Table View Inline Editing](images/37-table-inline-editing.png)\n\n### Fullscreen Issue Studio and Access Visibility Inspector\nExpanding any ticket unlocks the Fullscreen Issue Studio, featuring a Rich Markdown authoring toolbar, Sparkle 320ms Fill-in-the-Middle (FIM) ghost-text completion, the `\ud83d\udee1\ufe0f` Effective Access Inspector, and a 4-tab activity stream.\n\n![Fullscreen Issue View with Rich Markdown Toolbar and Access Inspector](images/39-fullscreen-issue-view.png)\n\n### Advanced Governance and Administrative Studios\nPlatform administrators manage enterprise governance through dedicated studios:\n- **AI Providers & Token Caps Studio (`/admin/ai`):** Write-only key custody, monthly token budgets, and air-gap policies (`images/43-admin-ai-studio-providers.png`).\n- **Invalid Object Link Auditor (`/admin/link-auditor`):** Continuous graph integrity verification, inspect drawer, and two-stage audited purge (`images/46-admin-link-auditor.png`).\n- **Workflow Transition Studio & Dry-Run Drawer (`/projects/:key/settings/workflows`):** Zero-persistence dry-run simulation with step timings and copyable CLI commands (`images/50-workflow-studio-dry-run-drawer.png`).\n- **Plane Migration Import Studio (`/admin/imports`):** Single-click bundle ingestion, dry-run diff preview, and transactional live migration (`images/49-admin-plane-import-studio.png`).\n\n![Admin Invalid Object Link Auditor Studio](images/46-admin-link-auditor.png)\n\n---\n\n## Architectural Distinctions: \ud83d\udc4dkanban vs Traditional Tools\n\n| Dimension | Legacy Trackers & Paywalled SaaS (Jira / Vibe Kanban) | \ud83d\udc4dkanban Platform |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **License & Cost** | Commercial SaaS / AGPL with paid AI paywalls | Pure Apache-2.0, zero paywalled features |\n| **Agent Interface** | 70-120 raw CRUD tool wrappers (15k-25k tokens) | 27 intent-driven MCP tools across 3 surfaces (<= 1.8k tokens for agent) |\n| **Database Security** | Application-layer authorization checks | Hardware-enforced PostgreSQL `FORCE ROW LEVEL SECURITY` on all tenant tables |\n| **Network Isolation** | Monolithic container or open Docker bridge | Hardened 5-network isolation matrix (`edge`, `app`, `data`, `sandbox`, `egress`) |\n| **Scripted Workflows & Helpers** | Basic webhooks with no blocking execution | Atomic synchronous Wasm validators/mutators and async AI agent gates |\n| **Input Sanitization** | Basic HTML strip | Hostile Unicode lone-surrogate rejection, hidden-DOM pruner, SVG sandbox |\n| **Deployment Mode** | Complex multi-service Kubernetes only | Single-container standalone (`docker run`) or full multi-container production |\n\nFor an exhaustive feature-by-feature evaluation across 35 criteria, see the [Feature Comparison Matrix](Feature-Comparison).\n\n---\n\n## Non-Bypassable Engineering and Security Invariants\n\n1. **Plain ASCII Hyphen Invariant:** All public documentation, wiki articles, and commit messages strictly mandate plain ASCII hyphens (`-`). Unicode em-dashes (U+2014) and en-dashes (U+2013) are strictly forbidden across the codebase and wiki.\n2. **Zero-Context Fail-Closed Database:** In the absence of an explicit session context (`SET LOCAL app.current_principal_id`), all queries against tenant tables return zero rows. The application role `kanban_app` is stripped of `SUPERUSER` and `BYPASSRLS`.\n3. **Hostile Unicode Rejection:** Text ingestion rejects UTF-16 lone surrogates (`0xD800` through `0xDFFF`) prior to UTF-8 encoding, preventing memory corruptions and parser desynchronization.\n4. **Paste-Jacking Defense:** Clipboard inputs are aggressively stripped of hidden-DOM payloads, zero-width spaces, and invisible injection sequences.\n5. **AAL2 Admin Route Enforcement:** Every endpoint under `/api/v1/admin/*` and every administrative tool on `/mcp/admin` requires Authenticator Assurance Level 2 (AAL2) credentials.\n6. **95% Automated Test Coverage:** All core modules maintain at least 95% unit test coverage running on clean-DB fixtures with sub-millisecond `SAVEPOINT` isolation.\n\n---\n\n## Complete Table of Contents\n\n### Track 1: Step-by-Step Guides\n1. [[Guide] Production Promotion and Backup Runbook](Production-Promotion-and-Backup-Runbook) - Single-command standalone promotion, encrypted KBBAK1 backup format, and disaster recovery.\n2. [[Guide] Legacy Tracker Migration and Cutover Runbook](Migration-and-Cutover-Runbook) - 7-phase zero-downtime cutover plan, dry-run reconciliation, and rollback procedures.\n3. [[Guide] How to Use Custom Fields](Guide-Custom-Fields) - Step-by-step custom fields guide, formulas, wasm/nsjail tiers, and approval workflows.\n4. [[Guide] Scripted Workflows and Transition Helpers](Scripted-Workflows-and-Transition-Helpers) - Synchronous transition validators/mutators and asynchronous AI agent gates.\n5. [[Guide] Multi-Card Authentication Studio and Identity Architecture](Multi-Card-Authentication-Studio) - Pluggable auth cards (OAuth2, LDAP, WebAuthn Passkeys, TOTP, Local Admin) with break-glass protection.\n6. [[Guide] Multi-Provider AI Engine, Execution Harnesses, and Runners](Multi-Provider-AI-Engine-and-Runners) - OpenAI, Ollama, Gemini integrations, local CLI pipe harnesses (`agy -p`, `codex -p`), and mTLS runners.\n7. [[Guide] Three-Surface Model Context Protocol (MCP) Server Architecture](Three-Surface-MCP-Server-Architecture) - Dedicated streamable endpoints (`/mcp/agent`, `/mcp/docs`, `/mcp/admin`) with InlineSafeDumper YAML.\n\n### Track 2: Feature & Field Reference\n1. [[Informational] Studio Configuration Reference](Studio-Configuration-Reference) - Exhaustive field configuration tables and security impact across all 11 \ud83d\udc4dkanban Studios.\n2. [[Informational] Enterprise Whitespace, Semantic Emojis, and Kanban Board](Enterprise-Whitespace-and-Kanban-Board) - 5 native view layouts, 2D swimlanes, sub-16ms drag-and-drop, and the `<EmojiHint>` semantic hover system.\n3. [[Informational] Ticket Screen, Peek Drawer, and Work Item Architecture](Ticket-Screen-and-Work-Item-Features) - 960px peek drawer, 17 enterprise work-item features, properties rail, and 4-tab activity stream.\n4. [[Informational] Hierarchical Docs, Project Stickies, and Smart Promotion](Hierarchical-Docs-and-Stickies-with-Smart-Promotion) - ltree page trees, color-coded sticky masonry, and lossless AI-assisted promotion to Docs.\n5. [[Informational] Blinking Cursor Sparkle Completion Engine](Blinking-Cursor-Sparkle-Completion-Engine) - Sub-300ms inline Fill-In-the-Middle (FIM) ghost text with surgical right-click disambiguation.\n6. [[Informational] Model Context Protocol (MCP) Tools Reference Manual](MCP-Tools-Reference) - Exhaustive specification of all 27 MCP tools, parameter schemas, LOD tiers, and destructive token workflows.\n7. [[Informational] REST API Architecture and OpenAPI Integration Guide](REST-API-Architecture-and-OpenAPI-Guide) - Technical guide to the 184-route FastAPI backend, interactive OpenAPI documentation, and TypeScript SDK.\n\n### Track 3: Security & Adoption Overview\n1. [[Informational] Role and Permission Matrix](Role-and-Permission-Matrix) - Visual \u25cf / \u25d0 / \u25cb role and capability matrix across all 7 principal tiers.\n2. [[Informational] Zero-Trust Security Architecture and Explicit Access Visibility](Zero-Trust-Security-and-Access-Visibility) - PostgreSQL FORCE RLS, dynamic sharing pill, access manifests, and STRIDE threat mitigation.\n3. [[Informational] Feature Comparison Matrix (35 Features)](Feature-Comparison) - Comprehensive capability comparison across 35 features evaluating \ud83d\udc4dkanban against Jira, Plane, GitHub, Vibe Kanban, Businessmap, and Codebeamer.\n\n### Track 4: Engineering & Security Architecture\n\n#### Functional Architecture\n1. [[Architectural] System Topology and Multi-Container Architecture](System-Topology-and-Multi-Container-Architecture) - Standalone embedded PostgreSQL Unix socket and 5-network production container stack.\n2. [[Architectural] Universal Object Graph and Invalid Link Auditor](Universal-Object-Graph-and-Link-Auditor) - Unified object spine, 13 typed object relationships, and automated invalid link detection/purging.\n3. [[Architectural] Real-Time Web and WebSocket Architecture](Real-Time-Web-and-WebSocket-Architecture) - Distributed WebSocket hub, connection throttling, channel subscriptions, and board state synchronization.\n4. [[Architectural] Canonical Markdown and Safe Media Pipeline](Canonical-Markdown-and-Safe-Media-Pipeline) - Hostile input sanitization, safe Mermaid rendering, SVG sandboxing, and media proxying.\n5. [[Architectural] Clean-DB Testing and Governance Gates](Clean-DB-Testing-and-Governance-Gates) - Fast parallel test execution, tmpfs template database, pluggable AI fixtures, and CI/CD validation.\n\n#### Security Architecture\n1. [[Architectural] Admin Custom Scripted Fields and Sandboxed Execution](Admin-Custom-Scripted-Fields-and-Sandbox) - Wasmtime (Tier A) and nsjail (Tier B) sandboxed execution with cryptographic tier escalation.\n2. [[Architectural] Custom Scripts and JSON Security Architecture](Custom-Scripts-and-JSON-Security-Architecture) - Hostile input sanitization, AST inspection, and ephemeral token boundaries.\n\n#### Engineering Appendix\n<details>\n<summary>Engineering Appendix</summary>\n\n- [[Architectural] \ud83d\udc4dkanban: Architecture Specification Delta & Gap Analysis](Architecture-Delta-and-Missing-Features) - Forensic analysis of specification requirements versus codebase implementation and tracking backlog.\n- [[Architectural] \ud83d\udc4dkanban User Task & Architecture QA Verification Matrix](User-Tasks-and-QA-Matrix) - Verification audit mapping tasks UT-01 through UT-16 to live browser checks and screenshot deliverables.\n\n</details>\n"
+    "content": "# \ud83d\udc4dkanban: Executive Architecture and System Overview\n\nWelcome to the authoritative technical documentation and wiki for **\ud83d\udc4dkanban** (`thumbs-up-kanban`), an open-source, enterprise-grade project management, ticketing, and knowledge platform built from the ground up on two fundamental pillars:\n1. **Security-First (Priority 0):** Hardened zero-trust infrastructure, PostgreSQL Row-Level Security (`FORCE RLS`), five-tier network isolation, AAL2 administrative authorization, and hostile input sanitization.\n2. **Agent-First (Priority 1):** Purpose-built for autonomous AI agents and human teams alike, replacing the context-bloating CRUD-wrapper anti-pattern with an intent-driven, three-surface Model Context Protocol (MCP) server, deterministic workflow gates, and sub-second execution loops.\n\nLicensed under the strictly permissive **Apache-2.0** license, \ud83d\udc4dkanban eliminates SaaS AI paywalls and per-seat subscription lock-in while competing globally against Jira, Vibe Kanban, and commercial issue trackers with drop-in enterprise migration support.\n\n---\n\n## System Topology\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart TD\n    subgraph Clients[\"Client Surfaces\"]\n        SPA[\"React 19 SPA (Desktop, Tablet, Mobile)\"]\n        Agents[\"Autonomous Agents (Cursor, Claude, Codex, Agy)\"]\n    end\n\n    subgraph Entrypoints[\"API & Protocol Gateways\"]\n        FastAPI[\"FastAPI Application Server<br/>- Multi-Card Auth (AAL2)<br/>- Canonical Markdown Pipe<br/>- WebSocket Realtime Hub<br/>- REST API (242+ routes, 316+ operations)\"]\n        MCP[\"3-Surface MCP Server<br/>- /mcp/agent (9 tools)<br/>- /mcp/docs (3 tools)<br/>- /mcp/admin (12 tools)<br/>- InlineSafeDumper YAML\"]\n    end\n\n    subgraph Core[\"Database Engine & Object Graph\"]\n        UOG[\"Universal Object Graph (UOG)<br/>PostgreSQL 16 with FORCE ROW LEVEL SECURITY (100%)<br/>- Typed object_links, Spine records, Append-only Ledger<br/>- ltree Hierarchical Docs, pgvector Embeddings, Full-Text<br/>- Invalid Object Link Auditor & Purger\"]\n    end\n\n    subgraph Runtimes[\"Execution Engines\"]\n        AIEngine[\"AI Engine & Orchestration<br/>- OpenAI, Ollama, Gemini<br/>- agy -p, codex -p pipes<br/>- Async Gate Helpers\"]\n        Sandbox[\"Sandbox Execution Runtime<br/>- Tier A: Wasmtime engine<br/>- Tier B: nsjail runner<br/>- Scoped Ephemeral Tokens\"]\n    end\n\n    SPA -->|HTTP / WebSocket| FastAPI\n    Agents -->|HTTP / SSE / STDIO| MCP\n    Agents -->|HTTP REST| FastAPI\n    FastAPI --> Core\n    MCP --> Core\n    Core --> AIEngine\n    Core --> Sandbox\n```\n\n---\n\n## Visual Tour: Platform Highlights\n\n### Enterprise Workspace and Project Hub\nThe workspace home delivers clear project visibility, team velocity metrics, and seamless multi-project navigation with responsive layouts across desktop, tablet, and mobile displays.\n\n![Workspace Home and Project Overview](images/05-workspace-home.png)\n\n### Breathable Whitespace Board and High-Contrast Theming\nThe core Kanban board features sub-16ms smooth drag-and-drop, semantic emoji hints, configurable WIP limits, and an enterprise dark theme for reduced eye strain during extended operational sessions.\n\n![Enterprise Whitespace Board View](images/06-board-view.png)\n\n![Dark Theme Enterprise Kanban Board](images/22-dark-theme-board.png)\n\n### Keyboard-Driven Command Palette\nGlobal keyboard shortcuts (`Ctrl+K` / `Cmd+K`) provide instant fuzzy navigation across tickets, documents, projects, and administrative studios without context switching.\n\n![Global Command Palette Navigation](images/23-command-palette.png)\n\n### Multi-View Projections: Table Inline Editing and Timeline Dependencies\nEngineers can switch instantly between Kanban Board, 3-pane List, Table with capability-gated inline cell editing, Calendar, and Timeline with SVG Bezier BLOCKS dependency arrows.\n\n![Table View Inline Editing](images/37-table-inline-editing.png)\n\n### Fullscreen Issue Studio and Access Visibility Inspector\nExpanding any ticket unlocks the Fullscreen Issue Studio, featuring a Rich Markdown authoring toolbar, Sparkle 320ms Fill-in-the-Middle (FIM) ghost-text completion, the `\ud83d\udee1\ufe0f` Effective Access Inspector, and a 4-tab activity stream.\n\n![Fullscreen Issue View with Rich Markdown Toolbar and Access Inspector](images/39-fullscreen-issue-view.png)\n\n### Advanced Governance and Administrative Studios\nPlatform administrators manage enterprise governance through dedicated studios:\n- **AI Providers & Token Caps Studio (`/admin/ai`):** Write-only key custody, monthly token budgets, and air-gap policies (`images/43-admin-ai-studio-providers.png`).\n- **Invalid Object Link Auditor (`/admin/link-auditor`):** Continuous graph integrity verification, inspect drawer, and two-stage audited purge (`images/46-admin-link-auditor.png`).\n- **Workflow Transition Studio & Dry-Run Drawer (`/projects/:key/settings/workflows`):** Zero-persistence dry-run simulation with step timings and copyable CLI commands (`images/50-workflow-studio-dry-run-drawer.png`).\n- **Plane Migration Import Studio (`/admin/imports`):** Single-click bundle ingestion, dry-run diff preview, and transactional live migration (`images/49-admin-plane-import-studio.png`).\n\n![Admin Invalid Object Link Auditor Studio](images/46-admin-link-auditor.png)\n\n---\n\n## Architectural Distinctions: \ud83d\udc4dkanban vs Traditional Tools\n\n| Dimension | Legacy Trackers & Paywalled SaaS (Jira / Vibe Kanban) | \ud83d\udc4dkanban Platform |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **License & Cost** | Commercial SaaS / AGPL with paid AI paywalls | Pure Apache-2.0, zero paywalled features |\n| **Agent Interface** | 70-120 raw CRUD tool wrappers (15k-25k tokens) | 24 intent-driven MCP tools across 3 surfaces (<= 1.8k tokens for agent) |\n| **Database Security** | Application-layer authorization checks | Hardware-enforced PostgreSQL `FORCE ROW LEVEL SECURITY` on all tenant tables |\n| **Network Isolation** | Monolithic container or open Docker bridge | Hardened 5-network isolation matrix (`edge`, `app`, `data`, `sandbox`, `egress`) |\n| **Scripted Workflows & Helpers** | Basic webhooks with no blocking execution | Atomic synchronous Wasm validators/mutators and async AI agent gates |\n| **Input Sanitization** | Basic HTML strip | Hostile Unicode lone-surrogate rejection, hidden-DOM pruner, SVG sandbox |\n| **Deployment Mode** | Complex multi-service Kubernetes only | Single-container standalone (`docker run`) or full multi-container production |\n\nFor an exhaustive feature-by-feature evaluation across 35 criteria, see the [Feature Comparison Matrix](Feature-Comparison).\n\n---\n\n## Non-Bypassable Engineering and Security Invariants\n\n1. **Plain ASCII Hyphen Invariant:** All public documentation, wiki articles, and commit messages strictly mandate plain ASCII hyphens (`-`). Unicode em-dashes (U+2014) and en-dashes (U+2013) are strictly forbidden across the codebase and wiki.\n2. **Zero-Context Fail-Closed Database:** In the absence of an explicit session context (`SET LOCAL app.current_principal_id`), all queries against tenant tables return zero rows. The application role `kanban_app` is stripped of `SUPERUSER` and `BYPASSRLS`.\n3. **Hostile Unicode Rejection:** Text ingestion rejects UTF-16 lone surrogates (`0xD800` through `0xDFFF`) prior to UTF-8 encoding, preventing memory corruptions and parser desynchronization.\n4. **Paste-Jacking Defense:** Clipboard inputs are aggressively stripped of hidden-DOM payloads, zero-width spaces, and invisible injection sequences.\n5. **AAL2 Admin Route Enforcement:** Every endpoint under `/api/v1/admin/*` and every administrative tool on `/mcp/admin` requires Authenticator Assurance Level 2 (AAL2) credentials.\n6. **95% Automated Test Coverage:** All core modules maintain at least 95% unit test coverage running on clean-DB fixtures with sub-millisecond `SAVEPOINT` isolation.\n\n---\n\n## Complete Table of Contents\n\n### Track 1: Step-by-Step Guides\n1. [[Guide] Production Promotion and Backup Runbook](Production-Promotion-and-Backup-Runbook) - Single-command standalone promotion, encrypted KBBAK1 backup format, and disaster recovery.\n2. [[Guide] Legacy Tracker Migration and Cutover Runbook](Migration-and-Cutover-Runbook) - 7-phase zero-downtime cutover plan, dry-run reconciliation, and rollback procedures.\n3. [[Guide] How to Use Custom Fields](Guide-Custom-Fields) - Step-by-step custom fields guide, formulas, wasm/nsjail tiers, and approval workflows.\n4. [[Guide] Scripted Workflows and Transition Helpers](Scripted-Workflows-and-Transition-Helpers) - Synchronous transition validators/mutators and asynchronous AI agent gates.\n5. [[Guide] Multi-Card Authentication Studio and Identity Architecture](Multi-Card-Authentication-Studio) - Pluggable auth cards (OAuth2, LDAP, WebAuthn Passkeys, TOTP, Local Admin) with break-glass protection.\n6. [[Guide] Multi-Provider AI Engine, Execution Harnesses, and Runners](Multi-Provider-AI-Engine-and-Runners) - OpenAI, Ollama, Gemini integrations, local CLI pipe harnesses (`agy -p`, `codex -p`), and mTLS runners.\n7. [[Guide] Three-Surface Model Context Protocol (MCP) Server Architecture](Three-Surface-MCP-Server-Architecture) - Dedicated streamable endpoints (`/mcp/agent`, `/mcp/docs`, `/mcp/admin`) with InlineSafeDumper YAML.\n\n### Track 2: Feature & Field Reference\n1. [[Informational] Studio Configuration Reference](Studio-Configuration-Reference) - Exhaustive field configuration tables and security impact across all 11 \ud83d\udc4dkanban Studios.\n2. [[Informational] Enterprise Whitespace, Semantic Emojis, and Kanban Board](Enterprise-Whitespace-and-Kanban-Board) - 5 native view layouts, 2D swimlanes, sub-16ms drag-and-drop, and the `<EmojiHint>` semantic hover system.\n3. [[Informational] Ticket Screen, Peek Drawer, and Work Item Architecture](Ticket-Screen-and-Work-Item-Features) - 960px peek drawer, 17 enterprise work-item features, properties rail, and 4-tab activity stream.\n4. [[Informational] Hierarchical Docs, Project Stickies, and Smart Promotion](Hierarchical-Docs-and-Stickies-with-Smart-Promotion) - ltree page trees, color-coded sticky masonry, and lossless AI-assisted promotion to Docs.\n5. [[Informational] Blinking Cursor Sparkle Completion Engine](Blinking-Cursor-Sparkle-Completion-Engine) - Sub-300ms inline Fill-In-the-Middle (FIM) ghost text with surgical right-click disambiguation.\n6. [[Informational] Model Context Protocol (MCP) Tools Reference Manual](MCP-Tools-Reference) - Exhaustive specification of all 24 MCP tools, parameter schemas, LOD tiers, and destructive token workflows.\n7. [[Informational] REST API Architecture and OpenAPI Integration Guide](REST-API-Architecture-and-OpenAPI-Guide) - Technical guide to the 242+ route FastAPI backend, interactive OpenAPI documentation, and TypeScript SDK.\n\n### Track 3: Security & Adoption Overview\n1. [[Informational] Role and Permission Matrix](Role-and-Permission-Matrix) - Visual \u25cf / \u25d0 / \u25cb role and capability matrix across all 7 principal tiers.\n2. [[Informational] Zero-Trust Security Architecture and Explicit Access Visibility](Zero-Trust-Security-and-Access-Visibility) - PostgreSQL FORCE RLS, dynamic sharing pill, access manifests, and STRIDE threat mitigation.\n3. [[Informational] Feature Comparison Matrix (35 Features)](Feature-Comparison) - Comprehensive capability comparison across 35 features evaluating \ud83d\udc4dkanban against Jira, Plane, GitHub, Vibe Kanban, Businessmap, and Codebeamer.\n\n### Track 4: Engineering & Security Architecture\n\n#### Functional Architecture\n1. [[Architectural] System Topology and Multi-Container Architecture](System-Topology-and-Multi-Container-Architecture) - Standalone embedded PostgreSQL Unix socket and 5-network production container stack.\n2. [[Architectural] Universal Object Graph and Invalid Link Auditor](Universal-Object-Graph-and-Link-Auditor) - Unified object spine, 13 typed object relationships, and automated invalid link detection/purging.\n3. [[Architectural] Real-Time Web and WebSocket Architecture](Real-Time-Web-and-WebSocket-Architecture) - Distributed WebSocket hub, connection throttling, channel subscriptions, and board state synchronization.\n4. [[Architectural] Canonical Markdown and Safe Media Pipeline](Canonical-Markdown-and-Safe-Media-Pipeline) - Hostile input sanitization, safe Mermaid rendering, SVG sandboxing, and media proxying.\n5. [[Architectural] Clean-DB Testing and Governance Gates](Clean-DB-Testing-and-Governance-Gates) - Fast parallel test execution, tmpfs template database, pluggable AI fixtures, and CI/CD validation.\n\n#### Security Architecture\n1. [[Architectural] Admin Custom Scripted Fields and Sandboxed Execution](Admin-Custom-Scripted-Fields-and-Sandbox) - Wasmtime (Tier A) and nsjail (Tier B) sandboxed execution with cryptographic tier escalation.\n2. [[Architectural] Custom Scripts and JSON Security Architecture](Custom-Scripts-and-JSON-Security-Architecture) - Hostile input sanitization, AST inspection, and ephemeral token boundaries.\n\n#### Engineering Appendix\n<details>\n<summary>Engineering Appendix</summary>\n\n- [[Architectural] \ud83d\udc4dkanban: Architecture Specification Delta & Gap Analysis](Architecture-Delta-and-Missing-Features) - Forensic analysis of specification requirements versus codebase implementation and tracking backlog.\n- [[Architectural] \ud83d\udc4dkanban User Task & Architecture QA Verification Matrix](User-Tasks-and-QA-Matrix) - Verification audit mapping tasks UT-01 through UT-16 to live browser checks and screenshot deliverables.\n\n</details>\n"
